/* Ethical Bridge CRM — Partnership Assessment Tool (PAT) question bank.
   109 questions in 8 scored areas, carried over unchanged from the previous CRM (28 Oct 2026).
   Scores: 1 major gaps · 2 limited · 3 partial · 4 mostly in place · 5 strong; N/A and blanks do not lower averages. */
export const PAT_SECTIONS=[{"n": 1,"title": "Qualification","short": "Qualification","questions": [{"id": "1:1","no": "1","cat": "Compliance","q": "Is the partner free from association with proscribed groups?","g": "Guide to Partner Vetting\n\nVetting approval verified on AMS"},{"id": "1:2","no": "2","cat": "Compliance","q": "Can the potential partner confirm that they have a zero tolerance approach to fraud, bribery, corruption and terrorism financing - as set out in policies - and can comply with applicable laws and SCI's policies? Is the partner willing to share serious incidents and/or breaches of fraud/corruption/safeguarding/terrorism financing with SCI?","g": "For which of these areas does the partner have controls and standards?  And what are those controls?\nHow are staff made aware of the partner's controls and standards, and how are they held accountable?\nDoes partner have a code of conduct that clearly sets standards and expectations for staff behaviour?\nCan the partner provide evidence of any examples of incidents, and how it responded to these?\n\n1. Partner policy & procedures - Fraud/Bribery/Corruption/Anti-Terror & Sanctions/Code of Conduct/HR policies/Safeguarding and procedures including for recruitment/screening/induction of staff and volunteers; whistleblowing or incident reporting procedure\n2. Previous due diligence completed by other NGOS/donors"},{"id": "1:3","no": "3","cat": "Compliance","q": "Have all child, adult, staff or volunteer safeguarding incidents or controversies which are publicly available (see sources of verification below) been adequately addressed by the organisation? Does the partner have effective controls and standards (that meet SC and donor requirements) for safeguarding, PSEA?","g": "Unaddressed incidents or controversies are an indication that the organisation does not have functioning safeguarding systems in place, and is likely to have an unsafe culture and integrity issues. As such, check if the partner has been reported in local or global media, as well as in any due diligence reference checks with other agencies, for safeguarding-related incidents and whether there is any evidence of inadequate response. In some situations, the partner may have made a public declaration, which should also be considered in your review.\n\n1.  Partner policy & procedures - Safeguarding (of staff & communities) / Code of Conduct / Modern Slavery/ HR policies and procedures, including for recruitment/screening of staff; health and safety policy \n2. Media reports"},{"id": "1:4","no": "4","cat": "Values","q": "Does the potential partner share Save the Children's values of Accountability, Ambition, Collaboration, Creativity, and Integrity, including on child and human rights?","g": "SC's values also include: neutrality, impartiality, child rights\n\nMission statement; Governing document; Organisational Charter; Annual Report"},{"id": "1:5","no": "5","cat": "Values","q": "Is the partner fair and unbiased in its work with communities?","g": "Any evidence of raised through external or internal sources?\n\nMission statement; Annual Report; Comments from third parties (other NGOs, community); media coverage"},{"id": "1:6","no": "6","cat": "Values","q": "Does the partner have access to, and credibility with, children and communities most affected by inequality and discrimination and/or with those whom the partner is seeking to influence?","g": "Any evidence raised through external or internal sources?\n\nMission statement; Annual Report; Comments from third parties (other NGOs, community); media coverage"},{"id": "1:7","no": "7","cat": "Legal","q": "Is the partner registered? For informal or child-led groups, are they recognised by the relevant authority or other civil society groups?","g": "Please note that an unregistered partner could encounter legal problems, so it is necessary to ensure evidence of a physical address and bank account details to ensure we are not putting the partner at risk.\n\nFor partners who are registered, partner legal registration document uploaded to AMS  \nFor unregistered partners, it is necessary to provide an Organigram and evidence of physical address and bank account details"},{"id": "1:8","no": "8","cat": "Legal","q": "Is the partner or key staff clear of any criminal investigations or pending court decisions?","g": "Any evidence of received through vetting or research through internal and external sources?\n\n1. Email from SCI Centre that vetting against Enforcement lists are clear/that there is no adverse media coverage OR if this is not the case, an email confirming risk mitigation strategy agreed with SCI Centre \n 2. Comments from third parties (e.g. other NGOS, donors)\n 3. Labour court or equivalent"},{"id": "1:9","no": "9","cat": "Capacity","q": "Does the partner have sound financial management and controls and fiduciary oversight?","g": "Are there any mentions of previously conducted audits and/or the ability to handle a donor audit?\n\n1. Latest audited financial accounts  \n2. Financial management policies, procedures and manuals \n3. Procurement/Asset management policies and procedures  \n4. Previous due diligence completed by NGOs/donors"},{"id": "1:10","no": "10","cat": "Capacity","q": "Does the partner do reputable, technically sound work?","g": "Any evidence of past performance or compliance issues?\n\n1. Formal reference/emails from third parties (e.g. peer local or INGOs, other entities such as multi-laterals or donors)  \n 2. Annual Report \n 3. Evaluations of previous work"},{"id": "1:11","no": "11","cat": "Neutrality","q": "Is the partner affiliated with any political parties or factions?","g": "Are any of the key persons or their relatives governmental officials or otherwise connected with politically-exposed persons? Is the partner affiliated with any political parties or factions? SC also expects shared respect for the principles of neutrality and impartiality, with partners not biased toward a specific political party or ethnic or demographic constituency.\n\nEmail from SCI Centre that vetting is clear OR if not, email confirming risk mitigation strategy agreed with SCI Centre"},{"id": "1:12","no": "12","cat": "Principles","q": "Are the partner’s leaders free of any potential conflicts of interest?","g": "Does the partner have a conflict of interest policy?  Do they know how to mitigate and manage conflicts of interest when they arise?\n\n1. Email from SCI Centre that vetting  is clear OR if not, email confirming risk mitigation strategy agreed with SCI Centre \n 2. Conflict of Interest policy (or Fraud Policy if that covers conflict of interest)"},{"id": "1:13","no": "13","cat": "Principles","q": "Is this partnership exposing partner staff to security risks and other risks that SCI would not expose their own staff to? Does going into partnership with SC cause any issues or risks for the partner?","g": "Are partner staff willing to work in an area where SCI staff do not go due to security concerns?  If the proposed partnership causes any  risks to the partner, it is recommended that SCI teams work with the partner to identify mitigation measures to these risks\n\nComments from partners"},{"id": "1:14","no": "14","cat": "Principles","q": "Is this partnership in line with SCI's 6 partnership principles?","g": "Will SC and the partner be able to implement the proposed partnership in line with SC's partnership principles? \nSC's partnership principles are: value driven and empowering relationships, transparency and accountability, mutual benefit and complementarity\n\nComments from partners"}]},{"n": 2,"title": "Scope of Work","short": "Scope","questions": [{"id": "2:1","no": "2.1","cat": "Scope of work","q": "What is the approximate amount of funding to be transferred under this partnership?","g": ""},{"id": "2:2","no": "2.2","cat": "Scope of work","q": "Who is the donor?","g": ""},{"id": "2:3","no": "2.3","cat": "Scope of work","q": "Health","g": ""},{"id": "2:4","no": "2.4","cat": "Scope of work","q": "Will the partner be implementing a Common Approach?","g": ""},{"id": "2:5","no": "2.5","cat": "Scope of work","q": "What geographic areas will the partner be expected to implement in?","g": ""},{"id": "2:6","no": "2.6","cat": "Scope of work","q": "Will the partnership be part of a humanitarian response?","g": ""},{"id": "2:7","no": "2.7","cat": "Scope of work","q": "Will the partnership include working with other downstream partners?","g": ""},{"id": "2:8","no": "2.8","cat": "Scope of work","q": "Will the project require the partner provide clinical health services?","g": ""}]},{"n": 3,"title": "Organizational Capacity","short": "Organisation","questions": [{"id": "3:1","no": "3.1","cat": "Governance and Leadership","q": "Does the partner have a documented, independent and functioning governance structure in place (with evidence of regular, minuted meetings)?","g": "Is there a conflict of interest/disclosure policy that assures the Board's independence from members of staff?\nWhat is the composition of the Executive Committee (EC)/Board? How does it function?\nHow many times did the EC/Board meet in the past year?\nWhat are the specific roles and actions that the EC performs to carry forward the mission of the organization?\nWhen did the partner last review the mission statement?"},{"id": "3:2","no": "3.2","cat": "Governance and Leadership","q": "Are senior management and/or Board adequately informed and supportive of the partnership and SOW?","g": "Has any correspondence been shared with senior management/Board regarding a potential partnership with SC?\nHas the SMT/Board issued any instructions regarding this potential relationship?\nHow does the SMT/Board stay abreast of other partnerships the organization is involved in?"},{"id": "3:3","no": "3.3","cat": "Governance and Leadership","q": "Are management and reporting lines clear and respected?","g": "Map out the organizational structure. For each of the key positions, show whether it is currently occupied, has an updated job description and well-established reporting line.\nAre there any variations between the structure on paper and how staff are supervised and managed on a day-to-day basis?"},{"id": "3:4","no": "3.4","cat": "Organisational Culture","q": "Does the partner demonstrate an awareness of and commitment to gender equality and diversity through its policies and procedures, and through the composition of its leadership and staff?","g": "Do key staff have an understanding of gender equality and measures the organization can take to foster it? Does the partner demonstrate a commitment to gender equality via their mission mandate policies and/or operating procedures? Does the partner align well with Save the Children Gender Equality Policy?  Is there a designated focal point for the policy? Can the partner describe how its organizational practices foster gender equality within the partner? Does the partner clearly demonstrate a commitment to equity and diversity within their team by having clear guidance/policies and balanced staff composition at all levels?"},{"id": "3:5","no": "3.5","cat": "Organisational Culture","q": "Does the partner value and promote inclusion, including undertaking anti-harrassement measures, fostering an environment that protects staff, volunteers and beneficiaries from discrimination, disrespect and any other form of inappropriate behaviour, including sexual harassment?","g": "Does the partner have a written policy or code of conduct against discrimination and harassment, approved by the relevant management body?\nDoes the partner provide awareness training to its members and staff on how to recognize and address forms of harassment?\nWhat mechanism and channels does the partner have to allow staff  and volunteers to report incidents safely and without fear of reprisal?\nHave there been reports of harassment, and what steps were taken to address them?"},{"id": "3:6","no": "3.6","cat": "Organisational Culture","q": "Does the partner undertake measures to ensure that the organization and its members and staff do not engage in or encourage any forms of modern slavery including trafficking in persons?","g": "Does the partner have a written policy or code of conduct against modern slavery, including trafficking in persons, approved by the relevant management body?\nDoes the partner provide awareness training to its members and staff on how to recognize and address forms of modern slavery?\nDoes the partner have a mechanism for reporting incidents of modern slavery?\nHave any such incidents been reported? What was the nature and what were the consequences?"},{"id": "3:7","no": "3.7","cat": "Child & Adult Safeguarding","q": "Does the partner have a written child and adult safeguarding policy and procedures, including protecting data about children, approved by the relevant management body?","g": "Is the policy written clearly, in local languages and distributed widely to all relevant stakeholders, including children? \nDoes the policy include a statement of the partner's commitment to child safeguarding, including a zero tolerance statement, that staff, volunteers and third parties should acknowledge and sign? \nDoes the policy include a code of conduct, risk assessment, guidance on recruitment, obtaining images and ICT, and measures to be taken if policy is breached?"},{"id": "3:8","no": "3.8","cat": "Child & Adult Safeguarding","q": "Are staff, volunteers, and all third parties and representatives of the organisation, as well as children and adults themselves, aware and supportive of the partner's commitment to keeping children and adults in the community safe from all forms of exploitation, abuse and harm?","g": "Do all members of staff, volunteers and associates receive mandatory training on safeguarding which describes how to recognise and respond to concerns in relation to the exploitation and abuse of children and adults, including sexual exploitation, abuse and harassment?\nDo they know how to recognize and respond to concerns about child abuse and poor practice which intentionally or unintentionally put a child at risk of harm or cause actual harm?\nAre children made aware of their right to be safe from abuse, and provided with advice and support on keeping themselves safe, including accessible information for children and parents/carers about where to go for help?\nPlease note: Standard corresponds with Core Operational Safeguarding Activity #6, 7 and 8, and will be annually reviewed with the Annual COSA Self-Assessment"},{"id": "3:9","no": "3.9","cat": "Child & Adult Safeguarding","q": "Does the partner have an appropriate process for reporting and responding to child and adult safeguarding incidents and concerns that fits with the local systems for dealing with incidents of exploitation, abuse and harm caused to children and adults by their staff, representatives and/or activities?","g": "Is there a designated Safeguarding Focal Point in partner? If not, who is responsible for safeguarding compliance from partner? \nDoes the partner have a whistleblowing policy which covers safeguarding issues?\nDoes the partner have accessible and safe reporting channels and mechanisms in place in each operational location?\nDoes the partner have clear investigation, case management and disciplinary procedures to use when allegations and complaints are made?\nIs the partner capable of handling child and adult safeguarding reports?\nHave any child and/or adult safeguarding incidents been reported? \nHave any safeguarding allegations been upheld?  What was their nature, and what were the consequences/action taken?\nPlease note: Standard corresponds with Core Operational Safeguarding Activity #10, 11 and 12, and will be annually reviewed with the Annual COSA Self-Assessment"},{"id": "3:10","no": "3.1","cat": "Child & Adult Safeguarding","q": "Has the partner put in place arrangements to monitor compliance with and implementation of child and adult safeguarding policies and procedures?","g": "Who is responsible for monitoring and reporting on the implementation of child and adult safeguarding and modern slavery policies?\nTo whom does s/he report, and how often? \nDo the partner keep a register of safeguarding issues raised and how they were dealt with? \nHave concerns/incidents been used as learning opportunities to improve policies and procedures? \nIs there a regulatory body to whom the partner must report any suspicions or concerns of child abuse? \nIf so, what is the name of the regulatory body and process?\n\nPlease note: Standard corresponds with Core Operational Safeguarding Activity #9. For each partner, an annual COSA Self-Assessment will need to be completed in cooperation with SCI and submitted by end of Q1 in order to review if standards are in place."},{"id": "3:11","no": "3.11","cat": "Risk Management","q": "Does the partner have strong risk management practices?","g": "Do they have a regularly updated and reviewed risk management plan?\nIs this on the senior leadership team’s standing agenda? \nDo they have a contingency budget?\nFor countries at high risk of aid diversion (according to SCI's Aid Diversion procedure), do they have strong mitigation tactics in place?"},{"id": "3:12","no": "3.12","cat": "Risk Management","q": "Does the partner follow sound data security practices?","g": "Will the partnership entail collection or storage of personal data?\nIs the policy written clearly, in local languages and distributed widely to all relevant stakeholders, including children?"}]},{"n": 4,"title": "Programme Capacity","short": "Programme","questions": [{"id": "4:1","no": "4.1","cat": "Thematic Capacities","q": "Does the partner have the thematic expertise needed for the project?","g": "Can key staff identify which positions are responsible for thematic expertise, and how they provide it to staff and projects?\nDo the relevant thematic staff have adequate expertise in the specific areas required by the SOW?\nDo the partner's current projects reflect thematic sophistication?\nWhere does the partner go when it needs additional thematic expertise?\nDoes the partner currently have available staff with the appropriate qualifications for the project's key positions?"},{"id": "4:2","no": "4.2","cat": "Thematic Capacities · Applies above US$100,000","q": "Does the partner have staff experienced in gender equality and inclusion/non-discrimination?","g": "Can the partner describe how its programs contribute to gender equality?\nHave the majority of partner staff been trained on gender equality and inclusion/non-discrimination?\nAre there key staff members who are specialists in these areas? \nDoes the partner ensure data are disaggregated by sex and age, and prioritize gender analysis as a key part of monitoring and evaluation?\nAre activities assessed to ensure that all children are safeguarded and included, including consideration of the needs of children who may have additional requirements to ensure their safe participation, such as those with different abilities, racial heritage, ethnic affiliations, religious belief, language, gender, those identifying as LGBTI, those with medical or physical conditions that may affect their participation (list is not exhaustive)?"},{"id": "4:3","no": "4.3","cat": "Thematic Capacities · Applies above US$100,000","q": "Does the partner have advocacy, media and communications experience adequate for the project?","g": "Can key staff describe the role that advocacy, media and communications play in supporting the organization, providing examples?\nHow do the partner's branding/communication initiatives promote visibility of the organization among key stakeholders?\nDoes the partner effectively use media (publications, website, public events, social media, etc.) to promote its mission and its constituents' interests?"},{"id": "4:4","no": "4.4","cat": "Project Management & Reporting · Applies above US$100,000","q": "Does the partner currently have available staff with the appropriate qualifications for the project's key positions?","g": "Can key staff describe the partner's approach to managing projects, e.g. whether it follows a centralized (i.e. project manager has line management of staff contributing to the project, including support service staff) or decentralized approach (i.e. project manager coordinates with functional units and site managers to get the support needed)? \nDo project managers have adequate authority and support to effectively manage projects?\nWill the partner need to staff up to assemble the needed project team?"},{"id": "4:5","no": "4.5","cat": "Project Management & Reporting","q": "Does the partner have staff with adequate reporting experience?","g": "Can the partner provide evidence of accurate, timely reporting (programmatic and financial) for previous projects?\nWhich staff are responsible for reporting, and how familiar are they with the projects?"},{"id": "4:6","no": "4.6","cat": "Project Management & Reporting","q": "Does the partner have the equipment and assets necessary to carry out the project?","g": "Can the partner provide evidence that it has the necessary equipment and assets (e.g. vehicles, office space and equipment, warehouse space), and that these will be available for use by the project when needed? \nAre the quality and quantity of assets appropriate for the project?\nCan the partner provide evidence that these assets are well maintained and managed by trained staff?"},{"id": "4:7","no": "4.7","cat": "Project Management & Reporting · Applies above US$100,000","q": "Are the partner's programmes designed, delivered and evaluated to prevent harm to children and achieve positive outcomes?","g": "Are programs consciously designed to prevent harm to children?\nDoes the partner deliver projects and services safely to children, in safe environments, and do they include general safety measures across thematic areas and contexts?\nDoes the partner monitor for child safety and child risk to ensure programs are safe for children?\nHave there been instances where children were harmed in a program? How was the program adapted as a result of the incident?"},{"id": "4:8","no": "4.8","cat": "Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability & Learning (MEAL)","q": "Does the partner have experience and skilled staff in monitoring projects?","g": "Does the partner have dedicated monitoring staff?\nCan the partner describe how it uses monitoring to support project management, and provide examples of monitoring plans for its projects?"},{"id": "4:9","no": "4.9","cat": "Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability & Learning (MEAL)","q": "Does the partner have monitoring tools and systems in place, include logframe, MEAL Plan, and Indicator Performance Tracking Table (IPTT)?","g": "Can the partner show evidence of routine use of well defined results-based indicators to track progress in achieving project objectives?"},{"id": "4:10","no": "4.1","cat": "Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability & Learning (MEAL)","q": "Does the partner have a system in place for Accountability to Children & Communities? If so, does it enable children and communities to have access to relevant and timely information; participate meaningfully and ethically in decision making; and have access to an inclusive and functioning Feedback and Reporting Mechanism (FRM)?","g": "Can the partner demonstrate that it ensures proper participation of the primary stakeholders, especially women, children and marginalized groups, in needs assessment, project design, project management and evaluation/learning? \nDoes the partner have accessible mechanisms to ensure that constituents, primary target groups, and other key stakeholders provide feedback (opinion, suggestions, concerns and complaints, etc.) on programs on a regular basis? Can the partner provide examples of beneficiary feedback it has received, and how it responded?"},{"id": "4:11","no": "4.11","cat": "Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability & Learning (MEAL) · Applies above US$100,000","q": "Does the partner have a system and culture of learning from its projects?","g": "Can the partner describe its practices to foster learning?  Who is involved?\nDoes the partner use research and evaluation findings to identify and raise issues relevant to its constituents?\nCan the partner describe how it links learning with its knowledge management?"},{"id": "4:12","no": "4.12","cat": "Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability & Learning (MEAL) · Applies above US$100,000","q": "Does this partner have experience leading or taking part in research, an evaluation, or an assessment?","g": "Can the partner demonstrate its experience through externally published reports?"},{"id": "4:13","no": "4.13","cat": "Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability & Learning (MEAL) · Applies above US$100,000","q": "Is the partner able to allocate at least 3% of the entire project budget (or staff capacity) to MEAL and ensure it accounts for all activities needed to meet MEAL requirements, including time to participate in SC MEAL trainings?","g": "Check against the proposed budget"},{"id": "4:14","no": "4.14","cat": "Advocacy and Campaigning","q": "Does the partner have clear and realistic plans and strategies to deliver its advocacy and campaign ambitions, when relevant to program implementation?","g": "Is the partner able to articulate a clear objective for its advocacy and campaign plan that has a reasonable chance of being achieved?\nIs the partner's advocacy and campaign objective linked to its programmes, and is it adequately resourced?\nDoes the partner have sufficient knowledge of strategies and activities to use for achieving the objectives?\nDoes the partner have a clear Monitoring and Evaluation plan that enables it to reflect on progress and challenges, and track the impact of its work?"},{"id": "4:15","no": "4.15","cat": "Advocacy and Campaigning","q": "Is the partner able to effectively engage with communities and key stakeholders on its advocacy and campaign issues, when relevant to program implementation?","g": "Has the partner developed its objectives in consultation with the affected communities and stakeholders?\nDoes the partner maintain strong links to the public and communities to maintain their engagement and support on achieving the objectives?\nIs there awareness throughout the most marginalised communities, including of gender and disability-specific implications of the current issues and proposed alternatives?"}]},{"n": 5,"title": "HR Capacity","short": "HR","questions": [{"id": "5:1","no": "5.1","cat": "Human Resource Management","q": "Does the partner have effective policies and procedures for staff recruitment, including means of screening for safe candidates?","g": "What policies and procedures does the partner have for recruitment and onboarding? What are the key stages of the process and who is responsible for the different stages?\nWhere does the partner announce its job vacancies?\nHow does the partner structure the interview and assessment process? How does the partner ensure there are no conflicts of interest in recruitment?  Is at least 1 interview question added to screen the attitude and suitability of candidate to work with children and adults at risk  from affected communities?\nHow does the partner assess a candidates attitude to anti-harassment and other forms of abuse within the workplace?\nWho makes the hiring decisions?\nWhat background checks and reference checks are done? Are police checks or references required? \nHow does the partner screen out anyone who may be unsuitable to work with children? Are employment references from official sources sought?\nHow long does a typical recruitment cycle take?\nPlease note:  standard corresponds with Core Operational Safeguarding Activity #4 on Safer Recruitment"},{"id": "5:2","no": "5.2","cat": "Human Resource Management","q": "Does the partner have effective policies and procedures for managing staff, including for staff compensation, performance management, development and retention?","g": "Can key staff describe the performance management cycle?  \nHow are new staff oriented to the organization?\nWhen and how are staff performances appraised?\nOver the past 12 months, how many staff have left, and why? \nDoes the partner have a duty of care policy or approach, documenting how it cares for its staff?"},{"id": "5:3","no": "5.3","cat": "Human Resource Management","q": "Does the partner have effective means of communicating with and soliciting feedback from staff?","g": "Give three examples of important decisions which the SMT has taken and how they were communicated with the rest of the organization?\nDoes the organization have regular all-staff meetings? Over the past three months, how many times have these meetings been held?\nDoes the partner have any mechanisms that enable staff to provide feedback or share ideas/feedback with management?\nHow does the partner communicate with staff who are based remotely, or outside the main office?"},{"id": "5:4","no": "5.4","cat": "Human Resource Management","q": "Does the partner have effective systems to safely attract, induct, deploy, manage and supervise volunteers for its work?","g": "How many volunteers has the partner engaged over the past year?\nHow does the partner register and monitor volunteers to ensure they know where they are at any given tme within the project/activity?\nDoes the partner have a procedure for screening, selecting, induction , placing and management of volunteers?\nDoes the organisation have a duty of care policy for volunteers? \nAre volunteers given clear job/role descriptions and do they have designated supervisors?\nDo volunteers receive orientation training, including on the organization's policies and ethics?\nAre volunteers actively supported and  supervised, and have any volunteers ever been dismissed?\nHow are volunteers motivated and recognized?\nPlease note:  standard corresponds with Core Operational Safeguarding Activity #4, and will be annually reviewed with the Annual COSA self-assessment."},{"id": "5:5","no": "5.5","cat": "Systems and Controls","q": "Does the partner demonstrate effective data security measures and controls, for both electronic and hard copy data?","g": "Can key staff describe what organizational data is sensitive and needs to be protected?\nCan key staff describe the partner's data security measures and controls, for both physical and electronic data?\nDo your observations confirm the partner's adherence to these measures and controls?\nWho is responsible for data security oversight? \nHas the partner ever faced data security breaches, and how did it respond?"},{"id": "5:6","no": "5.6","cat": "Systems and Controls · Applies above US$100,000","q": "Are there systems and practices in place for knowledge management, such as documentation of lessons learned or exit interviews for departing staff?","g": "Do key staff recognize the value of knowledge and documentation as key assets of the organization?\nDoes the partner have any written policy or procedures regarding knowledge management?\nCan the partner describe any specific practices it follows to retain knowledge?\nDoes the partner have any staff positions focused on knowledge management/ documentation, and are these  responsibilities written into staff members' job responsibilities?"},{"id": "5:7","no": "5.7","cat": "Systems and Controls","q": "Does the partner have adequate record retention practices and facilities to meet SCI's sub-award requirement for 10-year record retention?","g": "Does the partner have a record retention policy that aligns with SCI's requirements?\nWhat facilities or arrangements does the partner have for record retention?\nIf the partner has a physical archive, how secure, complete and organized does it appear to be?\nDoes the partner have confidence that it can retain a complete set of sub-award records on its premises for the 10-year period, or would it prefer SCI to retain these on its behalf?"}]},{"n": 6,"title": "Financial Capacity","short": "Finance","questions": [{"id": "6:1","no": "6.1","cat": "Planning and Budgeting · Applies above US$100,000","q": "Does the partner have an annual operating budget, which includes all expenses and revenue/income sources for all programs (with Board review and approval)?","g": "Are budgets prepared in timely fashion for all the costs of running the organisation?\nAre project budgets based on the costs of planned activities?\nDo budget worksheets include explanatory notes and clear calculations?\nIs a separate budget prepared for core costs (overheads)?\nIs a cash flow forecast prepared every month?"},{"id": "6:2","no": "6.2","cat": "Planning and Budgeting · Applies above US$100,000","q": "Does the partner have Financial Sustainability Plans in place?","g": "Does the partner monitor the trend of the pipeline awards?\nWhat proportion does the pipe form of the partner annual budget?\nHow many donors does the partner currently have? \nDoes the partner currently have a funding gap? What is the percentage if the funding gap against the current annual budget?"},{"id": "6:3","no": "6.3","cat": "Planning and Budgeting · Applies above US$100,000","q": "Does the partner have the capacity to work on cost-reimbursement basis?","g": "Does the partner have a specific need to be paid in advance?\nAre there donor requirements that would prevent this?"},{"id": "6:4","no": "6.4","cat": "Planning and Budgeting · Applies above US$100,000","q": "Are the right people involved in budgeting?","g": "Are both finance and programme staff involved in setting budgets?\nAre organisational budgets approved by the Board of Trustees?\nIs a named individual (budget holder) responsible for implementing and managing each budget?"},{"id": "6:5","no": "6.5","cat": "Planning and Budgeting · Applies above US$100,000","q": "Are budgets used for effective management?","g": "Do budget codes match (or correspond to) accounting codes?\nAre all planned operational costs adequately funded?\nIs a cash flow forecast prepared every month?"},{"id": "6:6","no": "6.6","cat": "Audit","q": "Does the Partner have an indirect cost sharing policy and evidence of how its calculated?","g": "Is it auditable?"},{"id": "6:7","no": "6.7","cat": "Basic Accounting System","q": "Are all transactions backed up by supporting documentation?","g": "Does every payment made have a supporting document providing evidence?\nAre all received cash or cheques recorded on pre-numbered carbon copy receipts?"},{"id": "6:8","no": "6.8","cat": "Basic Accounting System","q": "Are transactions properly recorded in the cashbook?","g": "Are all payments and receipts recorded in cashbooks (date, description, amount)?\nIs there a separate cashbook for each bank and cash account?\nIs every entry in the cashbooks cross-referenced to a supporting document?\nAre all cashbooks written neatly in permanent ink or on computer?"},{"id": "6:9","no": "6.9","cat": "Basic Accounting System","q": "Are the accounting books properly reconciled?","g": "Are all cashbooks updated at least once per month?\nIs a bank reconciliation done each month, for every bank account?\nIs a cash count reconciliation witnessed and recorded each month?\nDoes the partner keep track of amounts owed to others (e.g. suppliers) and owed by others (e.g. staff)?"},{"id": "6:10","no": "6.1","cat": "Basic Accounting System","q": "Are transactions properly coded?","g": "Is a standard Chart of Accounts used to code (or classify) each transaction in the cashbooks?\nAre transactions also classified by project or donor using a standard list of ‘cost centres’?"},{"id": "6:11","no": "6.11","cat": "Financial Reporting","q": "Are financial reports used for effective management?","g": "Do reports include details of cash and bank balances, amounts due (e.g. from staff) and owed (e.g. to suppliers)?\nDo budget monitoring reports include explanations and comments about differences?\nAre annual audits up to date (signed within 6 months of the year end)?\nAre financial reports used to help make decisions?"},{"id": "6:12","no": "6.12","cat": "Financial Reporting · Applies above US$100,000","q": "Are the right stakeholders receiving, reviewing and using financial reports?","g": "Does the Board review financial reports every quarter?\nDo senior managers discuss financial reports at least once every three months?\nDo budget holders receive budget monitoring reports every month?\nIs financial information shared with beneficiaries at least once per year, in an accessible way?"},{"id": "6:13","no": "6.13","cat": "Internal Controls · Applies above US$100,000","q": "Are there adequate measures to ensure that the organizational assets safeguarded?","g": "Is cash kept safely in a locked cashbox or safe, in the custody of one individual?\nIs all cash that is received banked intact, i.e. without any being spent?\nAre all fixed assets (e.g. vehicles, computers, equipment) that are owned by the NGO insured and controlled using a fixed assets register?"},{"id": "6:14","no": "6.14","cat": "Internal Controls","q": "Are accounting records accurate and up to date?","g": "Are bank reconciliations checked by someone who did not prepare them?\nAre statutory deductions (e.g. payroll taxes) properly made and paid on time?"},{"id": "6:15","no": "6.15","cat": "Internal Controls","q": "Are fraud and errors prevented and detected? Is there a fraud management (reporting, investigation and resolution) mechanism?","g": "Are all cheques signed by at least two authorised signatories?\nAre cheques signed only when all the details have been properly filled in (i.e. no signatories ever sign blank cheques)?\nAre staff salaries (including advances and loan deductions) checked each month by a senior manager?\nAre expense claims for staff advances checked by the same person who authorised the advance?\nIs a properly registered audit firm selected by the trustees?"},{"id": "6:16","no": "6.16","cat": "Internal Controls","q": "Are duties properly segregated to mitigate against risks and errors?","g": "Are cash payments authorised by someone other than the cashier?\nAre different steps in the procurement process, (e.g. ordering, receiving and paying) shared among different people?\nDoes the partner have a scheme of delegation that identifies limits of approval and signing authority of different senior staff?\nIs there an approved policies and procedures manual in place which is relevant to the organisation, and known by staff?"},{"id": "6:17","no": "6.17","cat": "Staffing","q": "Do staff have the right financial and accounting skills and qualifications?","g": "Does the Board include someone with the skills needed to oversee all financial activities?\nDo the finance staff have the skills (and qualifications) needed to carry out all financial activities?\nDo managers and programme staff have the financial skills they need to manage budgets and implement controls?\nDo all staff receive the training and support they need to carry out their financial management responsibilities?"}]},{"n": 7,"title": "Supply Chain Capacity","short": "Supply chain","questions": [{"id": "7:1","no": "7.1","cat": "Supply Chain Management","q": "Does the partner keep supply chain records? For how long?","g": "Can senior management identify critical supply chain documents that they maintain and for what length of time?\nDoes the partner's record retention policies meet the requirements of the donor?\nDoes the partner maintain a supply chain critical documentation checklist that meets SCI and Donor compliance requirements?"},{"id": "7:2","no": "7.2","cat": "Supply Chain Management","q": "Does the partner ensure that they conduct transparent, fair and sustainable supply chain activities?","g": "Does the Partner have a written code of conduct /policies/practices that promote:\n▫ Equal treatment of suppliers \n▫ Supplier selection based on fair competition\n▫ Segregation of duties in award and selection of suppliers \nDoes the partner take into account any sustainability or environmental considerations when selecting suppliers?"},{"id": "7:3","no": "7.3","cat": "Procurement","q": "Does the partner have supply chain roles that are directly responsible for procurement?","g": "Check that the partner has an organogram with supply chain roles /procurement roles with clearly defined interrelationships that provide adequate accountability to match the project requirements"},{"id": "7:4","no": "7.4","cat": "Procurement","q": "Does the partner have procedures in place for the procurement of goods and services?","g": "Does the partner have procurement standard operating procedures or procurement manual\nDoes the partner have valid framework agreements with prequalified or vetted suppliers\nDoes the partner have  a procurement purchase authorisation and spend threshold matrix \nDoes the partner use standardised forms /templates and or contract order forms \nDoes the partner complete project Procurement plans(recommended)"},{"id": "7:5","no": "7.5","cat": "Procurement","q": "Describe the procurement that the partner organisation has conducted on behalf of donors in the last 2 years. What was the value and what types of categories?","g": "Does the partner have significant donor spend experience (includes USAID, ECHO, OFDA, DFID)\nBased on likely procurement needs for the project - has the partner sourced/stored/moved goods/services related to the award already? \nDoes the partner have prior experience in managing specialist categories? (includes construction, cash, pharmaceuticals and specialised nutrition)"},{"id": "7:6","no": "7.6","cat": "Warehousing management and Operations","q": "Does the partner ensure that products can be safely received, adequately stored, and efficiently dispatched for program activities) including cold chain if required)","g": "Does the partner have an updated warehouse manual?\nDoes the partner have any certification of warehousing standards, for example ISO, GDP and or appropriate licenses from a government regulation body?\nDoes the partner carry out regular stock count/inventory count reports?\nDoes the partner keep stock management records, for example delivery notes, goods received notes, waybills, stock and ledger cards?\nDoes the partner regularly fumigate the warehouse and maintain fumigation schedule?\nDoes the partner have warehouse access control and keep access records?\nDoes the partner train warehousing staff and keep up to date staff training logs?\nIf the partner receives Gift in Kind donations how are they recorded and reported? What is the standard policy?"},{"id": "7:7","no": "7.7","cat": "Fleet management and Operations","q": "Does the partner have adequate fleet to meet the project requirements?","g": "What type and age of fleet does the partner own? Does partner adhere to local legislation requirements?\nDoes the partner keep up to date vehicle registration log books and driver’s license\nWhat type of rental contracts are in place to supplement the partner-owned fleet? Can contracts and service agreements be made available?"},{"id": "7:8","no": "7.8","cat": "Fleet management and Operations","q": "Does the partner have policies and or procedures in place to ensure vehicle safety and maintenance?","g": "Does the partner have vehicle maintenance logs\nDoes the partner maintain accident reports \nWhat safety & security measures are in place (e.g. maximum speed limits, mandatory use of seatbelts, guidelines for carrying of passengers, especially children etc.)? How are staff reminded of these (e.g. driver training, staff awareness & incident reporting)? Can this be evidenced, and if so, with what documentation?"},{"id": "7:9","no": "7.9","cat": "Fleet management and Operations","q": "Does the partner have policies or procedures partner in place for reporting accidents?","g": "Does the partner maintain and report accidents? Can this be evidenced, and if so, with what documentation?"},{"id": "7:10","no": "7.1","cat": "Fleet management and Operations","q": "Does the partner have procedures to ensure fuel is properly managed by drivers?","g": "What are the policies and processes for fuel management, including generators?  Can records be assessed with a clear audit trail?"},{"id": "7:11","no": "7.11","cat": "Asset management","q": "Does the partner have an asset management and disposal policy or procedure in place and what does it cover","g": "Does the partner have an asset management and disposal policy or procedure in place? Can an asset register be made available?\nHow is Asset authorization, recording, custody , of assets performed? Can this be evidenced by records e.g. custody forms?\nCan fixed assets be traced to the appropriate source of funds? Does the partner have physical asset tags?\nHow often does the partner conduct physical checks to verify and inspect assets, are there asset inspection records?\nHow does the partner account for lost, damaged or misplaced assets? Can this be evidenced by records for example lost assets records?"}]},{"n": 8,"title": "High-Risk Activities","short": "High risk","questions": [{"id": "8:1","no": "8.1","cat": "Major and Minor Construction Works","q": "It was reported in the Scope of Work section that this partnership wouldn't involve Construction activities, therefore, this question does not need to be answered.","g": ""},{"id": "8:2","no": "8.2","cat": "Major and Minor Construction Works","q": "It was reported in the Scope of Work section that this partnership wouldn't involve Construction activities, therefore, this question does not need to be answered.","g": ""},{"id": "8:3","no": "8.3","cat": "Major and Minor Construction Works","q": "It was reported in the Scope of Work section that this partnership wouldn't involve Construction activities, therefore, this question does not need to be answered.","g": ""},{"id": "8:4","no": "8.4","cat": "Major and Minor Construction Works","q": "It was reported in the Scope of Work section that this partnership wouldn't involve Construction activities, therefore, this question does not need to be answered.","g": ""},{"id": "8:5","no": "8.5","cat": "Major and Minor Construction Works","q": "It was reported in the Scope of Work section that this partnership wouldn't involve Construction activities, therefore, this question does not need to be answered.","g": ""},{"id": "8:6","no": "8.6","cat": "Major and Minor Construction Works","q": "It was reported in the Scope of Work section that this partnership wouldn't involve Construction activities, therefore, this question does not need to be answered.","g": ""},{"id": "8:7","no": "8.7","cat": "Procurement Procedures for Construction","q": "It was reported in the Scope of Work section that this partnership wouldn't involve Construction activities, therefore, this question does not need to be answered.","g": ""},{"id": "8:8","no": "8.8","cat": "Major Works Only","q": "It was reported in the Scope of Work section that this partnership wouldn't involve Construction activities, therefore, this question does not need to be answered.","g": ""},{"id": "8:9","no": "8.9","cat": "Major Works Only","q": "It was reported in the Scope of Work section that this partnership wouldn't involve Construction activities, therefore, this question does not need to be answered.","g": ""},{"id": "8:10","no": "8.1","cat": "Major Works Only","q": "It was reported in the Scope of Work section that this partnership wouldn't involve Construction activities, therefore, this question does not need to be answered.","g": ""},{"id": "8:11","no": "8.11","cat": "Award Specific Construction Risk","q": "It was reported in the Scope of Work section that this partnership wouldn't involve Construction activities, therefore, this question does not need to be answered.","g": ""},{"id": "8:12","no": "8.12","cat": "Award Specific Construction Risk","q": "It was reported in the Scope of Work section that this partnership wouldn't involve Construction activities, therefore, this question does not need to be answered.","g": ""},{"id": "8:13","no": "8.13","cat": "Cash and Voucher Assistance","q": "It was reported in the Scope of Work section that this partnership wouldn't involve CVA activities, therefore, this question does not need to be answered.","g": ""},{"id": "8:14","no": "8.14","cat": "Cash and Voucher Assistance","q": "It was reported in the Scope of Work section that this partnership wouldn't involve CVA activities, therefore, this question does not need to be answered.","g": ""},{"id": "8:15","no": "8.15","cat": "Cash and Voucher Assistance","q": "It was reported in the Scope of Work section that this partnership wouldn't involve CVA activities, therefore, this question does not need to be answered.","g": ""},{"id": "8:16","no": "8.16","cat": "Cash and Voucher Assistance","q": "It was reported in the Scope of Work section that this partnership wouldn't involve CVA activities, therefore, this question does not need to be answered.","g": ""},{"id": "8:17","no": "8.17","cat": "Cash and Voucher Assistance","q": "It was reported in the Scope of Work section that this partnership wouldn't involve CVA activities, therefore, this question does not need to be answered.","g": ""},{"id": "8:18","no": "8.18","cat": "Cash and Voucher Assistance","q": "It was reported in the Scope of Work section that this partnership wouldn't involve CVA activities, therefore, this question does not need to be answered.","g": ""},{"id": "8:19","no": "8.19","cat": "Cash and Voucher Assistance","q": "It was reported in the Scope of Work section that this partnership wouldn't involve CVA activities, therefore, this question does not need to be answered.","g": ""},{"id": "8:20","no": "8.2","cat": "Food Commodity Capacity","q": "Does the partner have the capacity to conduct in-kind food transfers, including associated procurement and distribution, based on previous experience?","g": "Gauging scale and capacity at scale"},{"id": "8:21","no": "8.21","cat": "Food Commodity Capacity","q": "Does the partner have policies or standard operating procedures that detail the process of site selection, taking into consideration, crowd control as well as beneficiary and staff safety and wellness?","g": "This gauges knowledge of mapping area of activity and site selection process and in line with sphere standards on safety and wellness."},{"id": "8:22","no": "8.22","cat": "Food Commodity Capacity","q": "Does the partner have polices or standard operating procedures that detail the process of transfer site management, including crowd control and establishing a process to assure efficient and safe transfers?","g": "This gauges knowledge of site management process and in line with sphere standards on safety and wellness."},{"id": "8:23","no": "8.23","cat": "Food Commodity Capacity","q": "Does the partner have monitoring systems in place to conduct on-site food basket monitoring?","g": "When conducting in kind transfers, random on site monitoring is standard to assure beneficiary are getting the appropriate entitlement. Note, this is different than post distribution monitoring."},{"id": "8:24","no": "8.24","cat": "Food Commodity Capacity","q": "Does partner have Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) or guidelines detailing practices from stock reception, storage, kitting, transport, distribution of food or agricultural commodities? Does the partner utilize tools or templates that track physical reception, storage, and transportation of commodities?","g": "This ensures procedures for minimum risk mitigation measures that aimed at preservation of stock from natural elements, pests, theft/loss, expiry, etc. and that there is auditable documentation for tracking commodity movements."},{"id": "8:25","no": "8.25","cat": "Asset management","q": "What is the partner’s current warehouse space capacity (in cubic metres) and type of commodities it is currently storing? What is current warehousing staffing structure in place overseeing warehouse stock?","g": "Speaks to current capacity and experience. Also gives idea whether current structure is fit for commodity type, value, volume etc."}]}];
